#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:792
#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:863
msgid "blowouts · Competitive+"
msgstr "一面倒比賽 · Competitive+"

#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:729
#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:797
#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:868
msgid "blowouts · random, no repeat"
msgstr "一面倒比賽 · 隨機、不重複"

#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:959
msgid ""
"Blowouts fade more slowly than quality: 52% one session in, 30% after two, "
"19% by round 50, 8% by round 100 — most of the way to the Oracle's 5% floor. "
"In a varied club they never fully go away: Competitive+ bottoms out near 35% "
"and even the Oracle blows out 23%, because a ringer and a beginner make some "
"matches unsaveable."
msgstr ""
"一面倒比賽消退得比品質慢：一次活動後 52%，兩次後 30%，第 50 輪時 19%，第 100 "
"輪時 8%——已接近 Oracle 的 5% 下限。在程度落差大的俱樂部裡，這種比賽永遠不會完"
"全消失：Competitive+ 最低約 35%，即使是 Oracle 也有 23%，因為高手與新手同場，"
"有些比賽本來就無解。"

#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:897
msgid ""
"Blowouts fade slowly in a varied room — they are not fully mitigated until "
"around round 100. A typical room reaches tight-room blowout rates within 30–"
"40 rounds."
msgstr ""

#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:355
msgid "click a strategy to isolate it"
msgstr "點選策略以單獨檢視"

#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingLab.re.mjs:108
msgid "Competitive+ (adaptive)"
msgstr "競技+ （自適應）"

#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingLab.re.mjs:106
msgid "Competitive+ (static)"
msgstr "競技+ （靜態）"

#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:410
msgid "Competitive+ match quality, by club"
msgstr "Competitive+ 的比賽品質（依俱樂部類型）"

#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:932
msgid "Conclusion"
msgstr "結論"

#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:876
msgid ""
"Concretely, in a typical room, switching a JP-style open play session to "
"Competitive+ is worth about 17 points of match quality and 16 points of "
"blowouts. Against a round-robin table it is worth about 9 and 7. Even in a "
"tightly curated private session, Competitive+ beats open play by about 11 "
"points of quality and 10 of blowouts. These are relative numbers from "
"synthetic rooms — and they are measured at round 100, with quality improving "
"roughly linearly along the way. Since Pkuru persists ratings across "
"sessions, the gains keep compounding."
msgstr ""

#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:1078
msgid "Could not load the data behind this article: {0}"
msgstr "無法載入本文的資料：{0}"

#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:768
msgid "Distance from truth — tight club"
msgstr "與真實值的差距——程度接近的俱樂部"

#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:907
msgid "Distance from truth — typical club"
msgstr "與真實值的差距——一般俱樂部"

#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:926
msgid "Distance from truth — typical club, with the Oracle"
msgstr "與真實值的差距——一般俱樂部（含 Oracle）"

#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:842
msgid "Distance from truth — varied club"
msgstr "與真實值的差距——程度落差大的俱樂部"

#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:847
msgid ""
"Early in my organising days I still switched from greedy, numerically "
"balanced matches to banded Competitive+. Banding forces every match to come "
"from a contiguous block of skill, even when that is numerically "
"“unbalanced”. A rating cannot capture everything about a real game: the best "
"and the worst player against two average players may balance mathematically, "
"but in practice it plays worse than an “unbalanced” match of three 4.0s and "
"a 5.0. Banding suppresses the measured quality score slightly because of "
"this override — that is the price of never pairing a ringer with a total "
"beginner just to make the numbers work out."
msgstr ""
"在我剛開始辦活動的日子裡，我仍從貪婪式、數值平衡的配對改用分段式的 "
"Competitive+。分段強制每場比賽都來自一段連續的實力區間，即使數值上看起來「不"
"平衡」。評分無法涵蓋真實比賽的一切：最強與最弱的球員對上兩位中等球員，數學上"
"或許平衡，但實際打起來比三位 4.0 加一位 5.0 的「不平衡」比賽更糟。正因為這種"
"凌駕機制，分段會略為壓低所測得的品質分數——這就是絕不為了湊數字而讓高手與完全"
"的新手同場的代價。"

#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:734
#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:802
#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:873
msgid "even games · Competitive+"
msgstr "勢均力敵的比賽 · Competitive+"

#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:739
#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:807
#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:878
msgid "even games · random, no repeat"
msgstr "勢均力敵的比賽 · 隨機、不重複"

#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:1145
msgid "every round a real ILP solve"
msgstr "每一輪都進行真正的 ILP 求解"

#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:980
msgid ""
"For a single court of five or six players, the rating system admittedly adds "
"little. The tool still helps: it remembers who has partnered whom, keeps "
"play counts even, and tracks each player's rating change round by round even "
"with nothing submitted — the session runs fairly, and everyone sees how they "
"actually did. People reliably overrate their own performance, even when they "
"do not show it."
msgstr ""
"若只有一面球場、五、六位球員，評分系統確實幫助有限。但工具仍然有用：它會記住"
"誰與誰搭檔過、讓上場次數平均，並逐輪追蹤每位球員的評分變化，即使沒有回報任何"
"成績——活動進行得公平，每個人也能看到自己實際的表現。人們總是可靠地高估自己的"
"表現，即使嘴上不說。"

#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:721
msgid ""
"From a cold start, Competitive+ pulls away from the random and round-robin "
"baselines around round 11 — roughly one three-hour session at six players "
"per court. A club of all-unrated players should expect their first session "
"to play no better than random while ratings are learned. After that, quality "
"compounds. By round 100 the gap is decisive:"
msgstr ""

#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:1002
msgid "Future improvements"
msgstr "未來的改進"

#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:698
msgid ""
"How the numbers were made: one simulation — 24 players, 4 courts, 100 rounds "
"— replayed across 7 seeds in three synthetic clubs: varied (skills spread "
"across the range, plus a ringer and a beginner), typical (about a 1.0 DUPR "
"spread), and tight (a bunched pack). True skills are not frozen: as in a "
"real club, about 20% of players improve gradually, one improves quickly — up "
"to half a DUPR point, with gains tapering as they settle — and one slowly "
"slips, the same players in every strategy's run so the comparison stays "
"fair. Every round is a real solve through the same optimiser the app uses. "
"Charts are 5-round rolling averages across all seeds; headline numbers "
"summarise the last 25 rounds. Timescales: a real session is 12–14 rounds, so "
"round 13 stands in for “one session” below, while the 100-round horizon — "
"seven or eight sessions of persisted ratings — shows the system once "
"everyone's rating is mature. Charts are interactive — hover for values, "
"click a strategy to isolate its line."
msgstr ""
"數據如何產生：一次模擬——24 位球員、4 個球場、100 輪——在三個合成球會中以 7 組"
"隨機種子重跑：多元型（實力分布廣泛，另加一位高手與一位新手）、典型型（DUPR 差"
"距約 1.0）與緊密型（實力集中）。真實實力並非固定不變：如同真實球會，約 20% 的"
"球員會逐步進步，一位進步迅速——最多提升半個 DUPR 分，增幅隨其穩定而遞減——另有"
"一位緩慢退步；每種策略的模擬皆採用相同球員，以確保比較公平。每一輪都經由 app "
"所使用的同一最佳化引擎實際求解。圖表為所有種子的 5 輪滾動平均；標題數字則彙整"
"最後 25 輪。時間尺度：實際一場活動約 12–14 輪，因此以下用第 13 輪代表「一場活"
"動」，而 100 輪的跨度——相當於七、八場活動累積的評分——則呈現所有人評分成熟後的"
"系統狀態。圖表可互動——游標懸停查看數值，點選策略可單獨顯示其曲線。"

#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:983
msgid ""
"If you are going to use a round robin table at all, use the Pkuru Round "
"Robin tool: the same table, better matches, every default tunable. And every "
"simulation in this article can be rerun for a club shaped like yours."
msgstr ""
"如果你無論如何都要用循環賽表，那就用 Pkuru 循環賽工具：同樣的表格、更好的對"
"戰、每項預設值皆可調整。而本文中的每一項模擬，都能依你球會的樣貌重新執行。"

#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:761
msgid ""
"In a tight club even the static Competitive+ profile keeps up with Balanced "
"Round Robin almost immediately: when everyone is close, a band drawn from "
"noisy ratings is barely different from one drawn from true skill, so banding "
"costs nothing here. The adaptive Competitive+ tracks Balanced Round Robin "
"from the first round by construction — it runs it until ratings settle. The "
"calibration phase earns its keep in the wider clubs below, where banding on "
"noise genuinely restricts the movement that would fix the ratings."
msgstr ""
"在緊密型球會中，即使是靜態的 Competitive+ 也幾乎立刻就能跟上 Balanced Round "
"Robin：當所有人實力相近時，依有雜訊的評分劃分的分級，與依真實實力劃分幾乎沒有"
"差別，因此分級在此毫無代價。自適應的 Competitive+ 在設計上從第一輪起就與 "
"Balanced Round Robin 一致——它會先執行後者，直到評分穩定。校準階段的價值展現在"
"下方實力較分散的球會，那裡依雜訊分級會實質限制原本能修正評分的流動。"

#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:773
msgid ""
"In the real world assembling a tight club of similarly skilled players is "
"challenging because on any given day a player's performance might fluctuate "
"by 0.5 points or more. The rating system however can adjust for this "
"variance within a few rounds of play."
msgstr ""
"在現實中，要組成一個實力相近的緊密型球會相當困難，因為球員在任何一天的表現都"
"可能起伏 0.5 分甚至更多。不過評分系統能在幾輪比賽內修正這種變異。"

#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:684
msgid "Inversion"
msgstr "評分倒置"

#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:764
msgid ""
"JP-style open play beats random slightly, most likely because it splits "
"obviously unbalanced foursomes — a behaviour I programmed in because "
"Japanese organisers actually do it. In the US that mixing often is not "
"there: players do not know each other well enough to restack a match, and "
"the ones who do are already clumped into a foursome."
msgstr ""

#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:826
msgid ""
"JP-style open play is the avoid-repeats baseline plus one intervention: a "
"foursome is split when it is obviously lopsided — the pairs half a DUPR "
"apart, the bar real organisers actually use. The surprise is that the "
"intervention buys nothing measurable: JP lands within the error bars of its "
"own baseline everywhere, a point or two of quality in this club at best. "
"Splits that rare cannot move a session. Politeness that fixes only the "
"egregious matches is worth almost nothing; the gains begin when every match "
"is deliberately balanced, which is exactly what nobody does socially."
msgstr ""
"日式開放打法是「避免重複」的基準做法，再加上一項介入：當一組四人明顯失衡時就"
"拆開——兩對相差半個 DUPR，這正是實際主辦者採用的標準。令人意外的是，這項介入沒"
"有帶來任何可衡量的效益：JP 在各處都落在自身基準的誤差範圍內，在這個球會頂多提"
"升一兩點品質。如此罕見的拆分無法改變一場活動。只修正極端失衡的客套做法幾乎毫"
"無價值；真正的收穫始於每一場對戰都被刻意平衡——而這正是社交場合中沒有人會做的"
"事。"

#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:962
msgid "Level-controlled clubs"
msgstr "分級管控的球會"

#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:1089
msgid "loading the precomputed run…"
msgstr "正在載入預先計算的結果…"

#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:715
#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:780
#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:854
msgid "Match quality"
msgstr "比賽品質"

#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:749
msgid "Match quality — tight club"
msgstr "對戰品質 — 緊密型球會"

#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:888
msgid "Match quality — typical club"
msgstr "對戰品質 — 典型球會"

#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:817
msgid "Match quality — varied club"
msgstr "對戰品質 — 多元型球會"

#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:1112
msgid "Matchmaking strategies, measured"
msgstr "配對策略實測"

#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:783
msgid ""
"Most open-play sessions in Japan are more varied than the organiser likes to "
"think: in the current pickleball scene it is hard to gather even one court "
"of genuinely similar players at once if only simply due to day-to-day skill "
"fluctuations."
msgstr ""
"日本多數的開放打球場次，比主辦者以為的更加參差：在當前的匹克球環境中，光是要"
"同時湊齊一個球場實力真正相近的球員都很困難，哪怕只是因為每天實力的自然波動。"

#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:1042
msgid "No precomputed run is published."
msgstr "尚未發布預先計算的結果。"

#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingLab.re.mjs:110
msgid "Open play (JP style)"
msgstr "開放打球（JP 風格）"

#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingLab.re.mjs:122
msgid "Open play (US style)"
msgstr "開放打球（US 風格）"

#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:986
msgid "Open the interactive Matchmaking Lab →"
msgstr "開啟互動式配對實驗室 →"

#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:688
msgid "Oracle"
msgstr "先知模式"

#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingLab.re.mjs:112
msgid "Oracle (knows truth)"
msgstr "神諭（知曉真相）"

#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:1011
msgid ""
"Our simulation currently handles players getting better and worse over time "
"(change in their true underlying skill), but it doesn't handle random "
"unrated drop in players that come back infrequently or never at all. It "
"should also fluctuate a player's skill between sessions (about every 13 "
"rounds) due to random day-to-day jitter in performance."
msgstr ""
"我們的模擬目前能處理球員實力隨時間變好或變差（真實底層實力的改變），但尚未處"
"理偶爾才回來、甚至再也不出現的無評分球員。它也應該加入場次之間（約每 13 輪）"
"因日常表現隨機波動而造成的實力起伏。"

#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:1101
msgid "Pkuru · matchmaking report"
msgstr "Pkuru · 配對報告"

#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingLab.re.mjs:116
msgid "Random (baseline)"
msgstr "隨機（基準）"

#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:482
msgid "random, avoid repeats"
msgstr "隨機、避免重複"

#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingLab.re.mjs:118
msgid "Random, avoid repeats"
msgstr "隨機，避免重複"

#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:758
#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:832
#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:897
msgid "Ratings convergence"
msgstr "評分收斂"

#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:1005
msgid ""
"Ratings keep sharpening for 30–40 rounds — two to three sessions — and while "
"the matchmaking is already better than the baseline by round 5, the first "
"dozen rounds of a true cold start remain the roughest stretch of a club's "
"life. I want to explore using score differentials to shorten them — "
"potentially producing usable ratings within a round or two of an unrated "
"player's first game. Currently the Round Robin tool already supports "
"manually specified player rankings. The risk is that this is itself a form "
"of oracle: reading more into a result than it actually says could tamper "
"with convergence rather than speed it up."
msgstr ""
"評分會持續精準化 30–40 輪——即兩到三場活動——雖然配對品質在第 5 輪就已優於基"
"準，但真正從零開始的頭十幾輪仍是球會生命中最顛簸的階段。我想探索用比分差距來"
"縮短這段期間——有機會在無評分球員打完一兩場後就產生可用的評分。目前循環賽工具"
"已支援手動指定球員排名。風險在於這本身也是一種先知模式：從結果中解讀出超過其"
"真實含意的資訊，可能會干擾收斂，而非加速它。"

#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:685
msgid ""
"Ratings pointing the wrong way: a strong player rated low, a weak player "
"rated high. Strong players who take it easy on beginners can invert their "
"own rating — unintentional sandbagging."
msgstr ""
"評分指向錯誤方向：強者評分偏低、弱者評分偏高。對新手手下留情的強者可能讓自己"
"的評分倒置——無意間的「藏分」。"

#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingLab.re.mjs:120
msgid "Round Robin"
msgstr "循環賽"

#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:835
msgid ""
"Round Robin and Balanced Round Robin lead early. Competitive+ catches up "
"after roughly 20 rounds and tracks Balanced Round Robin from there to round "
"100."
msgstr ""

#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:1163
msgid "Run these simulations yourself in the interactive lab →"
msgstr "在互動實驗室中自行執行這些模擬 →"

#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:1008
msgid ""
"Since we can simulate the match quality effects of adding a player into an "
"event, we can create an RSVP system that admits player based on their impact "
"to the session, rather than the simple first-come-first-serve setups most "
"events have."
msgstr ""
"既然我們能模擬加入某位球員對活動對戰品質的影響，就能打造一套依球員對場次影響"
"程度來錄取的報名系統，而非多數活動採用的先到先得制。"

#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:977
msgid "Single-court events"
msgstr "單場地活動"

#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:786
msgid ""
"The baseline here is what open play actually deals: random courts that avoid "
"repeating partners and opponents. (Measured against pure random, avoiding "
"repeats changes match quality not at all — novelty buys variety and a "
"slightly faster ladder, nothing else.) From a cold start, Competitive+ pulls "
"away from it within the first handful of rounds — by round 5 its games are "
"already measurably better, because every result moves a cold rating a long "
"way. Even a club of all-unrated players gets value inside their first "
"session, though in this club the early gain is match quality; the blowouts "
"barely move in one session, because preventing a varied club's worst games "
"takes ratings accurate enough to see them coming. With mature ratings the "
"gap is decisive:"
msgstr ""
"此處的基準是開放打法實際的安排方式：隨機分配球場，並避免重複的隊友與對手。"
"（相較於純隨機，避免重複完全不會改變對戰品質——新鮮感帶來的是變化與略快的排名"
"收斂，僅此而已。）從零開始，Competitive+ 在最初幾輪內就拉開差距——到第 5 輪其"
"比賽品質已明顯更佳，因為每筆結果都會大幅移動尚未穩定的評分。即使是全員無評分"
"的球會，也能在第一場活動內獲得價值，不過在這個球會中，早期的收穫是對戰品質；"
"懸殊比分在一場活動內幾乎沒有改善，因為要避免多元型球會中最糟的比賽，需要準確"
"到足以提前預見的評分。當評分成熟後，差距則相當決定性："

#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:974
msgid ""
"The idea that beginners and lower-rated players do not want balanced games "
"is a myth — in the US and Vietnam, DUPR round robins run routinely at the "
"2.0–3.0 levels. Everyone benefits from an even match, and no rating needs to "
"be at stake: the round robin tool can arrange matches by rating without "
"submitting results."
msgstr ""
"認為新手與低評分球員不想要勢均力敵比賽的想法是個迷思——在美國與越南，DUPR 循環"
"賽在 2.0–3.0 等級照樣定期舉行。人人都受惠於勢均力敵的對戰，而且不必拿評分冒"
"險：循環賽工具可依評分安排對戰，而不提交成績。"

#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:919
msgid ""
"The lesson for organisers: use manual seeding conservatively. The more you "
"pre-place players at their true level, the slower their rating gets there on "
"its own."
msgstr ""
"給主辦者的啟示：手動設定種子時要保守。你越是把球員預先擺在他們的真實水準上，"
"他們的評分自行到達那裡的速度就越慢。"

#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:916
msgid ""
"The Oracle knows everyone's real skill and hand-balances every match. It is "
"in the field to demonstrate one thing: rigging matches by what you know "
"prevents the ratings from ever learning it. Strong players are always split "
"and cancel each other out, so no informative result ever arrives — the "
"Oracle posts the best match quality of any strategy and the worst ladder "
"accuracy, stuck around seven places off forever. US-style open play's "
"starved ladder is the same effect arrived at by accident, in a milder dose."
msgstr ""
"先知模式知道每個人的真實實力，並親手平衡每一場對戰。它出現在測試中只為證明一"
"件事：依你已知的資訊操控對戰，會讓評分永遠學不到東西。強者總是被拆開並互相抵"
"銷，因此永遠不會出現有資訊價值的結果——先知模式的對戰品質是所有策略中最好的，"
"排名準確度卻是最差的，永遠卡在約七個名次的誤差。美式開放打法中「餓死」的排"
"名，正是同樣的效應在無意間、以較輕微的劑量發生。"

#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:1017
msgid ""
"This is a live document, so I will be updating the modelling, data, and "
"conclusions as they are discovered."
msgstr "這是一份持續更新的文件，我會隨著新發現不斷更新模型、數據與結論。"

#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:971
msgid ""
"This is where matchmaking lifts hardest. Blowouts are never fun — for the "
"stronger team they are a waste of time — and members you subject to them "
"often enough go elsewhere. Competitive+ prevents five of every six blowouts "
"in a typical club, halves them in a genuinely varied one, and its banding "
"lets a session holding a beginner group and an advanced group still resolve "
"into good matches instead of carry games."
msgstr ""
"這正是配對機制發揮最大效用之處。一面倒的比賽從來都不有趣——對強隊而言是浪費時"
"間——而經常被安排到這種比賽的會員往往會另尋他處。Competitive+ 在典型球會中可避"
"免六場一面倒比賽中的五場，在程度真正參差的球會中則可減半；其分級機制讓同時容"
"納初學組與進階組的場次仍能形成優質對戰，而非「帶飛」局。"

#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:675
msgid "Three terms worth pinning down"
msgstr "三個值得釐清的名詞"

#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:394
#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:537
msgid "Tight club"
msgstr "程度集中的球會"

#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:873
msgid ""
"Tight rooms give the best quality and the fewest blowouts, at some cost in "
"ranking accuracy — players who are genuinely close are hard to order. If you "
"can control the roster, keep the spread tight; even random matchmaking "
"performs decently there. If you cannot, Competitive+'s banding compensates: "
"a session holding a beginner group and an advanced group still resolves into "
"good matches."
msgstr ""

#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:712
msgid "Tight skill spread"
msgstr "程度差距小"

#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:669
msgid ""
"Two things decide which matchmaking strategy is best: the skill spread of "
"the club, and what you mean by “best”. Spread is how far apart your players "
"are in real ability. “Best” splits into two goals — keeping everyone in "
"tight, high-quality matches, and converging ratings to the truth quickly — "
"and while ratings are still unknown — somewhere in the first fifteen rounds, "
"about one session — you cannot have both. Faster convergence means injecting "
"randomness into the matchmaking, which costs match quality now; optimising "
"quality means trusting ratings that are still noise, which locks misrated "
"players in place. Some early time must be spent in exploratory, suboptimal "
"matches — unless you seed initial ratings by hand. Once ratings settle, the "
"tension mostly dissolves: the same strategy can hold the best match quality "
"in the field while converging as fast as anything else."
msgstr ""
"決定哪種配對策略最佳的因素有兩個：球會的程度分布，以及你如何定義「最佳」。分"
"布指的是球員實際能力的差距有多大。「最佳」可分為兩個目標——讓所有人都打到勢均"
"力敵的高品質比賽，以及讓評分快速收斂至真實水準——而在評分仍未明朗時（約前十五"
"輪，大約一場活動的時間），兩者無法兼得。加快收斂意味著在配對中注入隨機性，當"
"下的比賽品質便會下降；追求品質則意味著信賴仍充滿雜訊的評分，使被錯估的球員固"
"定在錯誤位置。除非你手動設定初始評分，否則早期必須花些時間在探索性、非最佳的"
"比賽上。一旦評分穩定下來，這種矛盾大致就消解了：同一套策略既能維持全場最佳的"
"比賽品質，收斂速度也不遜於其他任何方式。"

#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:851
msgid "Typical 3.0–4.0 spread"
msgstr "典型 3.0–4.0 程度分布"

#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:389
#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:539
msgid "Typical club"
msgstr "典型球會"

#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:829
msgid ""
"US-style open play — courts labelled by level, players choosing their own — "
"does somewhat better: matches only form within the stronger or the weaker "
"half of the club, so the skill gaps inside a match shrink. The simulation "
"also models the format's social habits — about half of badly beaten teams "
"run one revenge match, and close foursomes often stay on for another game; "
"both mean replaying a match, and the games people choose to replay are "
"usually the wrong ones. It nets out at 50% quality and 64% blowouts here, "
"against the baseline's 46% and 68% — real, but a long way from matchmaking "
"by rating, where Competitive+ reaches 66% and 35% in the same club. One "
"caution for anyone submitting rated DUPR matches from such sessions: repeats "
"and self-sorted courts carry little rating information, so they converge "
"ratings poorly — the simulated ladder ends up more than two places off, "
"against about one and a half for every other format."
msgstr ""
"美式自由開放打法——場地依程度標示、球員自行選擇——表現稍好：比賽只在球會中較強"
"或較弱的一半內形成，因此單場內的程度差距縮小。模擬也納入了這種形式的社交習慣"
"——約半數慘敗的隊伍會再打一場復仇賽，而勢均力敵的四人組常會續留再打一場；兩者"
"都意味著重複同一場對戰，而人們選擇重打的通常都是不該重打的那些。最終結果為品"
"質 50%、一面倒比賽 64%，相較基準的 46% 與 68%——確有改善，但距離依評分配對仍差"
"得遠：在同一球會中 Competitive+ 可達 66% 與 35%。若你打算將這類場次的比賽提交"
"為 DUPR 計分賽，需注意：重複對戰與自行分組的場地所含的評分資訊很少，因此評分"
"收斂很差——模擬中的排名最終偏離超過兩個名次，而其他所有形式約為一個半。"

#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:761
msgid ""
"US-style open play — courts labelled by level, players sorting themselves — "
"comes out worse than pure random on every measure, with a 60% blowout rate. "
"Two greedy individual behaviours explain it. Players who find a decent match "
"clump together and stay, stranding the leftover strong players in poorly "
"balanced games. And stacked teams like to run the “revenge” match, doubling "
"down on the bad matchup. A few lucky foursomes get good practice; the room "
"as a whole pays for it."
msgstr ""

#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:870
msgid ""
"Use Competitive+. The adaptive version handles the cold start with Balanced "
"Round Robin, then switches to banded play as ratings settle — the fastest "
"convergence available, with match quality at the top of the field."
msgstr ""

#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:935
msgid ""
"Use Competitive+. The adaptive version opens with Balanced Round Robin while "
"ratings are unknown, then switches to banded play as they settle — the "
"fastest convergence available, with the best match quality in the field. Two-"
"thirds of the gain arrives in the first session and most of the rest by the "
"end of the second (63% → 73% → 79% quality in a typical club), and because "
"ratings persist, each session starts where the last one left off."
msgstr ""
"使用 Competitive+。自適應版本在評分未明時以平衡循環賽開場，待評分穩定後切換為"
"分級對戰——收斂速度最快，比賽品質也是全場最佳。三分之二的效益在第一場活動就會"
"顯現，其餘大部分在第二場結束時到位（典型球會品質為 63% → 73% → 79%），而且由"
"於評分會保留，每場活動都能承接上一場的成果。"

#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:384
#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:542
msgid "Varied club"
msgstr "程度參差的球會"

#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:777
msgid "Varied skill levels"
msgstr "程度差異大"

#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:1014
msgid ""
"We have access to live match data from real sessions that use Round Robin "
"tool, including match scores. That means I can calculate the effects of "
"things like asymmetrical matches or the actual efficacy of the algorithms."
msgstr ""
"我們能取得使用循環賽工具的真實場次即時比賽數據，包括比分。這代表我可以計算諸"
"如不對稱對戰的影響，或演算法的實際成效。"

#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:938
msgid ""
"What switching is worth, with mature ratings in a typical club: 23 points of "
"match quality and blowouts cut from 59% to 10% against JP-style open play "
"(which plays like dealing at random); 7 points and 18 fewer blowouts against "
"a plain round-robin table; 17 points and 42 fewer against a curated private "
"session run as open play."
msgstr ""
"在評分成熟的典型球會中，改用它的價值：相較日式自由開放打法（其表現形同隨機分"
"配），比賽品質提升 23 分，一面倒比賽從 59% 降至 10%；相較普通循環賽表，品質提"
"升 7 分、一面倒比賽減少 18 個百分點；相較以自由開放形式進行的精選私人場次，品"
"質提升 17 分、一面倒比賽減少 42 個百分點。"

#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:680
msgid ""
"When everyone is close in skill, rating-based matchmaking has little to add "
"at first. Competitive+ only starts to pull away from round robin around "
"round 16, and the gains stay minor until about round 30 — in a tight room, "
"almost any way of dealing the courts produces decent games."
msgstr ""

#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:913
msgid "Why the Oracle never converges"
msgstr "為何 Oracle 永遠不會收斂"

#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:968
msgid "Wide-level open plays"
msgstr "程度跨度大的自由開放打法"

#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:857
msgid ""
"With a realistic 1.0-DUPR spread, Competitive+ pulls away from the baselines "
"within the first handful of rounds, and one session in it already leads the "
"avoid-repeats baseline by 9 points of quality and 10 points of blowouts. The "
"full benefit arrives with mature ratings: 10% blowouts against the "
"baseline's 62%, and a 78% chance of an even game against 53%. Those mature "
"numbers match a hand-picked tight-skill club (79% and 8%) — the algorithm "
"recovers by matchmaking what you would otherwise get by gatekeeping the "
"roster:"
msgstr ""
"在實際的 1.0 DUPR 分布下，Competitive+ 在最初幾輪內就拉開與各基準的差距，一場"
"活動下來已比「避免重複」基準高出 9 分品質與 10 分一面倒比賽表現。完整效益在評"
